=== Scope and known warnings ===
Direct-chain worlds run until 6.2 seconds so a projectile emitted at 2.85 seconds can use its actual three-second lifetime.
The initial 4.2-second cleanup assertion failed after the blast moved the source away from the backstop; no game lifetime was shortened to satisfy the test.
Initial diagnostic FVector fields were zero-initialized before the final run; the erroneous first-run uninitialized control diagnostic is not treated as gameplay motion.
Positive/negative movement fixtures stop at 0.9 seconds; physics and normal timers run through actual World::Tick with dt=0.01, once per automation frame.
The test directly activates only initial starters. Target activation always comes from actual ProjectileMovement Sweep and BallisticReactive; target movement is Chaos/column/impulse settlement.
Native Pawn source/damage uses the existing automation character; formal enemy AI/firing remains T14.
SavedBlueprintNaturalChain actually flies a projectile from saved emitter to saved bomb. SavedRangeConfiguration only loads/verifies map configuration, not gameplay in the map.
Saved map has five manual stations and fourteen Dormant devices, with tagged BlockAll / WorldStatic ground. No automatic linked activation or target teleport is authored.
Current graphical Murdock PIE/manual timing, formal enemies/drops, capacity, complete-round restart, independent package, frame-rate/long-run checks and complete G2 remain pending.
Final map commandlet has eight existing Paragon Rig/input mapping warnings. Existing ClearIgnoredActors compilation warning and user ABP_MothMurdock divide-by-zero warning are not fixed by this task.
No Git push or new PR is performed; T12 local work is not added to the still-open T10/T11 PR #39.

